<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTD/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  M14-04 residual: liveness LaunchAgent TEMPLATE for the nightly backup.
  Runs at 09:00 and alerts unless a fresh artifact exists. Installation is
  operator-manual (see docs/RUNBOOKS.md "Backup & restore"): copy this file to
  ~/Library/LaunchAgents/, substitute the two placeholders, then
  `launchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ...`.

  Placeholders (the operator fills these in at install; nothing host-specific
  is committed):
    __HOME__             absolute home dir       (e.g. /Users/<you>)
    __REPO_ROOT__        absolute repo checkout  (e.g. /Users/<you>/code/careerforge)
    __BACKUP_DIR__       absolute backup destination on the removable card
                         (e.g. /Volumes/<CARD>/careerforge-backups)
    __BACKUP_CARD_ID__   the opaque id written into the card sentinel at the
                         VOLUME ROOT (e.g. /Volumes/<CARD>/.careerforge-card)
    __KURA_BIN__         absolute path to the kura executable
                         (e.g. /Users/<you>/.local/bin/kura)
    __KURA_PROJECT_BACKUPS__  kura project name for the backup directory
    __KURA_PROJECT_BUS__      kura project name for the ops-bus bundle

  __KURA_BIN__ is absolute because launchd starts this job with
  PATH=/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin and the `-l` login shell sources .zprofile
  but not .zshrc - so a tool in ~/.local/bin is on PATH in every shell an
  operator would test in and invisible here. Measured from a real run, not
  assumed. PATH itself is deliberately NOT overridden: node lives on it too,
  and replacing it wholesale to fix kura would risk losing the dependency this
  check cannot do without.

  The kura project names are ARGUMENTS, not environment (M16-10 D24): which
  replication legs this agent watches is then visible in the agent definition
  itself rather than buried in a variable. Remove them and the intel leg is
  reported as NOT CHECKED in the log - never silently passed over. If a site
  runs no intel leg at all, install with no extra arguments and the check
  covers the card leg only, saying so on every line.

  M16-10 D24/D35: BACKUP_DIR and BACKUP_CARD_ID are supplied HERE, in
  EnvironmentVariables, and the script resolves the process environment FIRST
  and .env only as a fallback. Both must be present for the card-identity check
  to mean anything: BACKUP_DIR alone answers "is there a directory", and only
  the sentinel comparison answers "is it the RIGHT card", which is the
  distinction D3 exists to draw. TZ carries the IANA zone, never a fixed offset
  and never a bare "CDT", so this job's log stamps follow DST by themselves.

  Mirrors com.careerforge.backup.plist deliberately: ProgramArguments (not
  Program) so the Login Items UI shows a meaningful name, and BOTH
  StandardOutPath and StandardErrorPath so a raw interpreter error cannot land
  in the log without its matching stdout context - the 2026-08-13/14 false
  alarm was harder to read because only stderr was captured.

  NOTE ON WHY THIS RUNS AT ALL: the check reads the backup share through node,
  because under a launchd agent macOS TCC denies readdir() to shells while
  permitting it to node. Full measurement is in the script header. Do not
  "simplify" the listing back to `ls` - it will silently report an empty
  directory and alert every morning.

  Output is value-free by construction (filenames, counts, ages only), so
  logging to ~/Library/Logs is safe.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.careerforge.backup-liveness</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
      <string>__REPO_ROOT__/scripts/launchd/careerforge-backup-liveness</string>
      <string>__KURA_PROJECT_BACKUPS__</string>
      <string>__KURA_PROJECT_BUS__</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>__REPO_ROOT__</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
      <key>BACKUP_DIR</key>
      <string>__BACKUP_DIR__</string>
      <key>BACKUP_CARD_ID</key>
      <string>__BACKUP_CARD_ID__</string>
      <key>BACKUP_KURA_BIN</key>
      <string>__KURA_BIN__</string>
      <key>TZ</key>
      <string>America/Chicago</string>
    </dict>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
      <key>Hour</key>
      <integer>9</integer>
      <key>Minute</key>
      <integer>0</integer>
    </dict>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/careerforge-backup-liveness.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>__HOME__/Library/Logs/careerforge-backup-liveness.log</string>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>
  </dict>
</plist>
